Bloom: add libkvazaar10, an HEVC Main 10 encoder over a 10-bit build of Kvazaar.

Kvazaar fixes its sample depth when it is compiled (KVZ_BIT_DEPTH), and FFmpeg's libkvazaar
wrapper opens the 8-bit API with 4:2:0 8-bit input only. Bloom builds Kvazaar a second time for
10-bit samples, with every external symbol renamed to kvz10_ so both static archives link into the
one libavcodec, and installs it as the kvazaar10 pkg-config package with the public header
<kvazaar10/kvazaar10.h>.

The wrapper is parameterized by LIBKVAZAAR_BIT_DEPTH: libkvazaar.c keeps the 8-bit libkvazaar
encoder, and libkvazaar10.c compiles the same wrapper against the 10-bit header as libkvazaar10
(4:2:0 10-bit input, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P10). The frame copy and the block padding of patch 0001 now
work in kvz_pixel units, so both builds share them. Kvazaar writes the Main 10 profile itself from
its sample depth. libkvazaar10 is registered after libkvazaar, so the default HEVC encoder is
unchanged; configure gains --enable-libkvazaar10.

